  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Relief for IDPs &amp; Vulnerable Communities in Yei Diocese</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The July 8th. 2016 conflict in Juba had considerable repercussion in Yei River State. Many young men took arms to defend themselves against armed offensive by government army in the State. Thousands of civilian population fled into the bushes and into neighbouring countries of Uganda and DR Congo. The insurgency and the conflict caused appalling humanitarian situation in the entire Yei River State. Food, health, protection and education situation became despicable. Hundreds of homes were abandoned, looted and burnt. Tens of thousands people were displaced. Many lives were lost. All roads to and from Yei Town were closed. As time passed the resilience of the people of Yei was weakened and humanitarian aid becomes imperative to rescue lives and to reduce displacement and refuge. UN-WFP was obligated to carry out &#x201C;blanket food aid distribution&#x201D; in October 2016.</narrative>
  </description>
